    "answer": {
      "short": "$m\\le-\\dfrac72$ or $m\\ge\\dfrac72$.\n\nThe angular interval must cover at least one full revolution.",
      "worked": "The identity gives the unit circle:\n$$x^2+y^2=\\cos^2(mt)+\\sin^2(mt)=1.$$\nThe angular interval has length $|m|\\frac{4\\pi}{7}$. The entire circle is described exactly when this is at least $2\\pi$:\n$$\\begin{align*}|m|\\frac{4\\pi}{7}&\\ge2\\pi\\\\|m|&\\ge\\frac72\\end{align*}$$\nHence $m\\le-\\frac72$ or $m\\ge\\frac72$. Negative $m$ reverses the direction of traversal.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
